From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:45:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-uvm: don't end a compound statement with a label

uvm_gpu_map_cpu_pages_for_egm() has a label right before #else, which
compilers without C23 label rules (GCC < 11, e.g. on EL8) reject: "label at
end of compound statement". Add an empty statement.

Fixes upstream issue 1390.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c
index ffff835d..6d42f184 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-uvm/uvm_gpu.c
@@ -4108,6 +4108,7 @@ NV_STATUS uvm_gpu_map_cpu_pages_for_egm(uvm_parent_gpu_t *parent_gpu,
         atomic64_add(size, &parent_gpu->mapped_cpu_pages_size);
 
 done:
+        ;
 #else
         status = NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED;
 #endif
